{
  "id": "22504_neagesuru",
  "headword": "{値上|ねあ}げする",
  "reading": "ねあげする",
  "romaji": "neagesuru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb-suru",
  "gloss": "to raise prices; to mark up",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to raise prices; to mark up",
      "explanation": "To increase the price or cost of goods or services."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22504_neagesuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{電気代|でんきだい}が{値上|ねあ}げされた。",
      "english": "Electricity prices were raised.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22504_neagesuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{店|みせ}は{毎年|まいとし}{値上|ねあ}げしている。",
      "english": "This store raises prices every year.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22504_neagesuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{原材料|げんざいりょう}の{高騰|こうとう}により、{商品|しょうひん}を{値上|ねあ}げせざるを{得|え}なかった。",
      "english": "Due to soaring raw material costs, they had no choice but to raise prices on their products.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers specifically to raising prices, as opposed to prices rising on their own. The noun form {値上|ねあ}げ is commonly used on its own to mean 'a price increase.'\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {家賃|やちん}を{値上|ねあ}げする: to raise the rent\n- {料金|りょうきん}を{値上|ねあ}げする: to raise fees\n- {大幅|おおはば}に{値上|ねあ}げする: to raise prices significantly\n- {一斉|いっせい}{値上|ねあ}げ: across-the-board price increase\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {値下|ねさ}げする: to lower prices — the opposite action\n- {値上|ねあ}がりする: to go up in price — describes prices rising by themselves, without specifying who raised them\n- {高|たか}くなる: to become expensive — a more general and casual expression",
